      "summary": "\n\nHere are the key takeaways from last night's NBA action (June 22, 2025):\n\n*   **Shai Gilgeous-Alexander (Thunder):** 29 points on 8-of-27 shooting (2-of-12 from 3), 12 assists, 5 rebounds, and 2 blocks in 40 minutes. Despite the poor shooting efficiency, he drove the Thunder to a 103-91 victory over Indiana with a +11 plus/minus.\n*   **Chet Holmgren (Thunder):** 18 points on 6-of-8 shooting, 8 rebounds, and a game-high 5 blocks in 31 minutes. His rim protection anchored the Thunder's defensive effort in the win.\n*   **Bennedict Mathurin (Pacers):** 24 points and 13 rebounds (7 offensive) in 33 minutes. He was perfect from the free-throw line (10-of-10) but struggled from the field (6-of-14), finishing with a -14 plus/minus in the loss.\n*   **T.J. McConnell (Pacers):** 16 points on 8-of-13 shooting and 6 rebounds, but his night was marred by 7 turnovers in 28 minutes of action.\n*   **Aaron Nesmith (Pacers):** 3 points on 1-of-5 shooting, but contributed 6 rebounds, 2 steals, and 2 blocks in 30 minutes. He was one of the few Pacers with a positive impact, finishing at +6.\n*   **Alex Caruso (Thunder):** 10 points on 4-of-10 shooting, 3 steals, and 1 block off the bench. He provided strong two-way energy in 32 minutes, contributing to the Thunder's +8 plus/minus.",
